{
    "README": "Shared fixture for the automatic sector grid. buildSectorGridCells() (includes/functions-warroom.php) and gridCellsForPolygon() (assets/js/war-room-utils.js) are the same algorithm written twice - the server creates the sectors, the client previews them and tells the coordinator how many are coming. Both are asserted against this one file, by tests/SectorGridFixtureTest.php and tests/js/sector-grid.test.js, so the day one side is changed without the other, CI says so. Counts are compared exactly; coordinates with a 1e-6 tolerance (about 11cm), because PHP and JS round the last decimal place differently and no operation on the ground cares. Regenerate with the scratchpad generator only after the behavioural tests in tests/SectorGridTest.php still pass - this file records what the algorithm does, it is not the definition of what it should do.",
